# Mythos audit 2026-04-30 — config_adjustments.json is RUNTIME STATE
# (the running config tuner's history of approved adjustments), not
# source. Tracking it in git meant any checkout/reset could silently
# wipe the working state — exactly what happened on 04-29 when 200
# entries went to 5 (HEAD's old version). Untracked + atomic-rotated
# (.bak) is enough; recovery is via .bak, not git.
.claude/config_adjustments.json
.claude/config_adjustments.json.bak
# Mythos audit 2026-05-04 — operator-triggered TUI snapshots ('c' hotkey).
# Paste-back diagnostic artifacts containing live runtime state, never source.
.claude/snapshots/
# Mythos 2026-04-30 — brain feed disk tee (runtime observability,
# rotates at 5MB to feed.jsonl.1, never source-controlled)
.claude/brain/feed.jsonl
.claude/brain/feed.jsonl.1
